---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import ContactBand from '../components/ContactBand.astro';
---

<Base
  title="About — Zeltranet"
  description="Zeltranet is an independent software engineering company based in Mexico and Laos, working with businesses in Mexico, Laos, Thailand, Malaysia, and internationally."
>
  <section class="page-intro container">
    <h1>
      Independent engineering.
      <br />
      Connected thinking<span class="blue-text">.</span>
    </h1>
    <p>
      Zeltranet is an independent software engineering company based in Mexico
      and Laos, serving business customers in Mexico, Laos, Thailand, Malaysia,
      and internationally. We work in English and Spanish, across time zones
      from the Americas to Southeast Asia.
    </p>
  </section>
  <section class="container about-content">
    <h2>
      Built around
      <br />
      business needs.
    </h2>
    <div>
      <p>
        Software should make everyday operations clearer and more reliable. We
        focus on the systems behind the work: the applications people use, the
        information they depend on, and the processes that connect them.
      </p>
      <p>
        Our work brings together software engineering, systems integration, and
        practical AI automation. The aim is straightforward: help businesses
        operate more efficiently with software they can understand and maintain.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="container about-content founder">
    <div>
      <span class="eyebrow">THE FOUNDER</span>
      <h2>
        Maximiliano
        <br />
        Brito Torres.
      </h2>
    </div>
    <div>
      <p>
        Zeltranet was founded by Maximiliano Brito Torres (Maxon), a software
        engineer who has built and maintained software for businesses since
        2015, in Mexico, Thailand, China, and Laos.
      </p>
      <p>
        Maxon has worked as a developer for software companies and a bank in
        Bangkok, taught web development at universities in China and Laos, and
        managed software projects for a technology company in Vientiane. That
        work was done for those organizations, not as Zeltranet engagements; it
        shapes how Zeltranet approaches engineering.
      </p>
      <a class="text-link" href="https://maxontorres.com" rel="noopener">
        maxontorres.com <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span>
      </a>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="container approach-section">
    <span class="eyebrow">ENGINEERING PRINCIPLES</span>
    <div class="approach-grid">
      <article>
        <h2>Clarity before complexity.</h2>
        <p>
          Understand the problem and choose technology that serves it. A simpler
          system is often easier to operate and improve.
        </p>
      </article>
      <article>
        <h2>Reliability by design.</h2>
        <p>
          Account for failures, maintenance, and the people who will use the
          software every day.
        </p>
      </article>
      <article>
        <h2>Practical collaboration.</h2>
        <p>
          Keep scope, tradeoffs, and progress visible, explained in plain
          language. Good engineering depends on shared understanding.
        </p>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>
  <ContactBand />
</Base>
